    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras are leaning heavily on speed-indexed matchups today, headlined by **Trea Turner** (75.89) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (72.94). **Trea Turner** is our premier play, benefiting from a high-leadoff spot and a 94% stolen base success rate probability against Dollander\u2019s slow delivery. Similarly, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** earns a massive boost from a 100% SB probability projection; despite hitting 8th, his matchup against Rocker combined with his dynamic speed profile makes him a mandatory start in our pursuit of category scarcity. **Kyle Schwarber** (69.69) also offers high upside in the same game as **Trea Turner**, anchored by a robust 0.394 xwOBA that justifies his slot in the two-hole against a vulnerable pitching matchup.\n\nOur decision-making process for the utility spots was tight, with **Yordan Alvarez** (57.92) and **Junior Caminero** (56.98) barely edging out the rest of the fringe starters. While **Yordan Alvarez** faces a significant platoon disadvantage against the left-handed Lodolo, his elite 0.425 xwOBA floor keeps him in the mix; conversely, **Junior Caminero** gains a favorable wind-out environment that offsets the threat of Early\u2019s SP_xERA of 3.03. **Carson Benge** (56.44) represents the most interesting bench-adjacent choice, as his consistent platoon edge against right-hander Nelson secures his spot over potential utility depth. We are monitoring **Gary Sanchez** (49.29) and **Kazuma Okamoto** (47.74) closely, as their scores are hampered by tough SP matchups against Fried and Detmers respectively. With **Christian Yelich** sidelined on the IL and **Zac Veen** still refining his approach in Albuquerque, we are operating with a lean active roster, making every efficient plate appearance from **Caleb Durbin**\u2014whose score is propped up by a wind-out advantage despite a bottom-of-the-order designation\u2014vital for our daily efficiency caps.",
